.TH tkutltree n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutltree
.PP
Convert between nested data and a \fBtablelist\fR tree, with free column
mapping. A node is a dict of named fields plus an optional list of child nodes;
\fB\-fields\fR maps field names to columns in order.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutltree::fromData tbl data -fields {f ...} ?-childrenkey children? ?-parent root?
::tkutils::tkutltree::toData   tbl       -fields {f ...} ?-childrenkey children? ?-node root?
::tkutils::tkutltree::clear    tbl ?-node root?
.CE
.SS "Data model"
.PP
Each node: \fB<field> <value> ...\fR plus an optional \fBchildren\fR
(configurable) list of child nodes. \fB\-fields\fR (required) names the columns
in order; missing fields become empty cells. \fBfromData\fR/\fBtoData\fR
round\-trip is stable.
.SS "Error codes"
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLTREE <REASON>}\fR (FIELDS, OPTION).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tkutils::tkutablelist(n)
.SH KEYWORDS
tablelist, tree, dict, hierarchy
